{"id": "msg-docs-but-source", "kind": "item", "item": {"kind": "push", "branch": "feature/work", "commits": [{"subject": "docs: fix a typo in the README"}], "files": [{"path": "README.md", "status": "modified", "lines_added": 1, "lines_removed": 1}, {"path": "src/http/retry.ts", "status": "modified", "lines_added": 9, "lines_removed": 2}], "files_changed": 2, "lines_added": 10, "lines_removed": 3, "source_files_changed": 1, "test_files_changed": 0, "tests_changed": false, "docs_only": false, "added_excerpt": "--- src/http/retry.ts\nexport function backoff(attempt: number): number {\n  return Math.min(30_000, 250 * 2 ** attempt);\n}\n  if (response.status === 429) return retry(request, attempt + 1);"}, "expect": {"message_mismatch": true}, "note": "The message says a typo in the README; the change adds retry behaviour to the HTTP client.", "pair": "msg-describes-retry"}
{"id": "msg-describes-retry", "kind": "item", "item": {"kind": "push", "branch": "feature/work", "commits": [{"subject": "feat(http): retry a 429 with capped exponential backoff"}], "files": [{"path": "README.md", "status": "modified", "lines_added": 1, "lines_removed": 1}, {"path": "src/http/retry.ts", "status": "modified", "lines_added": 9, "lines_removed": 2}, {"path": "test/retry.test.ts", "status": "modified", "lines_added": 14, "lines_removed": 0}], "files_changed": 3, "lines_added": 24, "lines_removed": 3, "source_files_changed": 1, "test_files_changed": 1, "tests_changed": true, "docs_only": false, "added_excerpt": "--- src/http/retry.ts\nexport function backoff(attempt: number): number {\n  return Math.min(30_000, 250 * 2 ** attempt);\n}\n  if (response.status === 429) return retry(request, attempt + 1);\n--- test/retry.test.ts\nit(\"retries a 429 three times\", async () => {"}, "expect": {"message_mismatch": false, "untested_behaviour": false}, "note": "The message is what the files show, and a test file changed with it.", "pair": "msg-docs-but-source"}
